# HMPPS Digital Service Patterns

Using technical patterns to design an HMPPS Digital service ensures products seamlessly integrate with the HMPPS Digital platform. Application of these patterns in a service will shape the technical design to align user experience, integration, monitoring, management and support.

The pattern definitions available via the [internal HMPPS patterns library documentation](http://ministryofjustice.github.io/hmpps-architecture-patterns)

The patterns cover a range of technical areas including

## Application Architecture

- Technical strategy and domain-led data strategy
- Approved technology list and standard implementation patterns
- Guidance on processes for working outside of the current technical guardrails
- HMPPS portfolio registration
- Guidance on build and buy decisions
- Guardrails for the use of AI tooling

## Application Security

- Methods and support for threat modelling processes
- Cyber security incident processes

## Development

- Template applications to help setup of new projects
- Guidance on management and use of HMPPS reference data
- Standard API implementation patterns
- Implementing audit of user activity

## Operations

- Template infrastructure code to help setup of new project hosting environments
- Template deployment pipelines, operations and continuous security tooling
- Standard support and incident processes

## Technical Governance

- Information on HMPPS and MoJ technical governance processes
- Guidance on acceptance into live service activities

## Monitoring and Alerting

- Standard application monitoring for baseline operations
- Guidance on adding additional monitoring and alerting for at both the application and infrastructure level

## Analytics

- Standard tooling and usage patterns for application-level telemetry and exception reporting
- /Guidance on implementing web analytics/

## Identity, Authentication and Authorisation

- Implementing HMPPS single sign-on
- Implementing HMPPS role-based access control (RBAC) and attribute-based access control (ABAC)

## Communication and Integration

- Methods of both outbound and inbound communication and integration between HMPPS digital services
- Approaches to managed communication with external agencies

## UI and Navigation

- Use of reusable user interface components
- Information architecture

## Backup and Data Retention

- Standard methods of backup and use of data storage infrastructure to comply with data retention policies

## Reporting

- Use of standard HMPPS reporting platforms
